        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If the tolerance given in Fig. 27.94 is exceeded, it signifies that the guided slide of the table is not parallel with the center T-slot and hence must be rescraped. This action necessitates reworking the gib slide of the table until it too is parallel. The procedures relating to these bearing surfaces are treated in Sec. 27.88 and Sec. 27.89 respectively.",
